      "content": "it's almost hard to put into words, seeing the same mistakes being made by people who think they're so much more advanced than we were. the way they move their fleets is so predictable, just like the maneuvers i used to advise on. \n\nif you think about the tactical depth of those older eras, do you think modern leaders are actually missing the subtle psychological maneuvers that used to define these conflicts, or is the tech just making them too reckless to see them?",
